{"id":"n-20261022-5u7s6l","category":"sports","display_title":"Portland Opens Season With Dominant Win","display_title_he":"פורטלנד פותחת עונה בניצחון מרשים","short_summary":"Portland started the new NBA season with a commanding 124-83 victory over Phoenix, featuring standout performances from Damian Lillard, Ja Morant, and Israeli forward Deni Avdija.","english_level":"C1","words":497,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Portland%2C_Oregon%2C_US_-_August_2025_-_109.jpg/960px-Portland%2C_Oregon%2C_US_-_August_2025_-_109.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Another Believer · CC BY-SA 4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portland,_Oregon,_US_-_August_2025_-_109.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"Walla","domain":"sports.walla.co.il","url":"https://sports.walla.co.il/item/3873286","title":"טוב שבאתם: פורטלנד פתחה עונה עם תצוגת תכלית מול פיניקס","published_at":"2026-10-22T07:22:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-22T07:22:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-22T06:17:19.944Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The Portland Trail Blazers commenced the 2026/27 National Basketball Association season in spectacular fashion, securing a comprehensive 124-83 victory over the Phoenix Suns at the Moda Center. Unlike the previous campaign, during which Israeli star Deni Avdija frequently had to shoulder the immense burden of carrying the team almost single-handedly, the opening night demonstrated a striking shift in the roster's overall balance and competitive depth.","The tone for the evening was set immediately as the hosts overwhelmed the visitors with an astonishing twenty-one to zero scoring run at the very beginning of the contest. This staggering burst represented the largest opening run by any team in the league over the past twenty-five seasons. Phoenix failed to convert a single field goal for more than six minutes, allowing Portland to establish a commanding forty-three to twelve advantage by the conclusion of the first quarter. The thirty-one-point differential matched the franchise record for the highest-scoring opening period in club history, while a thirty-three-point halftime margin set a new franchise benchmark for a season opener.","Damian Lillard dominated the headlines in his triumphant return to regular-season action for the franchise after missing the entire previous year due to a severe Achilles tendon injury sustained during his stint in Milwaukee. Playing just twenty-four minutes, the veteran guard accumulated twenty-five points while shooting six of ten from beyond the three-point arc. He also contributed six assists and converted all five of his free throw attempts, highlighting his remarkable comeback with a logo three-pointer among his twelve first-quarter points.","Meanwhile, new acquisition Ja Morant provided a fascinating glimpse into the team's high-ceiling potential. Operating alongside Lillard, the newly arrived playmaker orchestrated the offense effectively while registering fourteen points, five rebounds, and eight assists. His plus-thirty-three differential stood as the highest on the team, though his play also led to a brief on-court confrontation with Phoenix guard Devin Booker that resulted in a technical foul for both players.","For Deni Avdija, playing his third season in Portland, the evening proved uniquely liberating. While he still delivered a solid double-double consisting of eighteen points, ten rebounds, and four assists, he was not required to generate virtually every offensive play by himself. With Morant directing operations and Lillard commanding defensive attention, the ball circulated fluidly, enabling the squad to distribute thirty-2 total assists compared to a modest twenty-five point one average from the prior season.","Head coach Mike Nuri celebrated a successful debut in his new position, while the collective statistics underscored the overwhelming nature of the triumph. Portland outrebounded Phoenix sixty-eight to forty-four, aided by ten rebounds from Robert Williams and seven from Donovan Clingan, and sank nineteen three-pointers at a forty point four percent clip. Devin Booker served as the primary bright spot for the visiting side with twenty-three points, supported by ten points each from Dillon Brooks and Jalen Green, but the visitors ultimately proved entirely helpless against the relentless defensive intensity and offensive versatility displayed by the home team throughout the blowout encounter."],"facts":[{"fact":"Portland Trail Blazers defeated Phoenix Suns 124-83 in their 2026/27 season opener.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Deni Avdija recorded a double-double with 18 points and 10 rebounds.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Damian Lillard returned from an Achilles tendon injury with 25 points and six three-pointers after missing the previous season.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Ja Morant contributed 14 points and 8 assists in his debut for Portland.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Portland opened the game with an unprecedented 21-0 run, leading 43-12 after the first quarter.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Portland","lemma":"Portland","pos":"noun","he":"פורטלנד","name":"Portland"},{"text":"Trail","lemma":"Trail","pos":"noun","he":"טרייל","name":"Trail"},{"text":"Blazers","lemma":"Blazers","pos":"noun","he":"בלייזרס","name":"Blazers"},{"text":"commenced","lemma":"commence","pos":"verb","he":"התחילו","name":null},{"text":"National","lemma":"National","pos":"adjective","he":"לאומית","name":null},{"text":"Basketball","lemma":"Basketball","pos":"noun","he":"כדורסל","name":null},{"text":"Association","lemma":"Association","pos":"noun","he":"התאחדות","name":null},{"text":"season","lemma":"season","pos":"noun","he":"עונה","name":null},{"text":"spectacular","lemma":"spectacular","pos":"adjective","he":"מרשים","name":null},{"text":"fashion","lemma":"fashion"